## Summary

I fixed three TypeScript errors in `src/services/contentstack.ts` that were blocking the Live Preview SDK integration:

1. **`host` and `management_token` type errors (lines 82-83)**: The `contentstack.Config`'s `LivePreview` interface requires `host: string` and `management_token: string` (non-optional). The previous attempt used `|| undefined` which produced `string | undefined`, failing tsc. I replaced the inline `live_preview` object with a conditional spread — the entire `live_preview` block is only included when `CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_ENABLED === "true"`, at which point `host` and `management_token` are passed as plain `string` values (defaulting to `""` from the destructured env vars). This mirrors the existing conditional spread pattern already used for `CONTENTSTACK_FETCH_TIMEOUT`.

2. **`stack` property error (line 107)**: `@contentstack/live-preview-utils`'s `IInitData` interface declares `stackSdk: IStackSdk`, not `stack`. Changed `ContentstackLivePreview.init({ stack: Stack })` to `ContentstackLivePreview.init({ stackSdk: Stack })`.

All three prescribed helpers remain in use: `ContentstackContext` and `useContent` are consumed in `_app.tsx`, and the `ContentstackContextProvider` subscribes to `onEntryChange` to propagate draft content through the existing `getContentByKey` pipeline. No tests were written (test authorship belongs to the dedicated test-writer agent).

