## Root cause of the verification failure
`src/services/contentstack.ts` had a **static** `import ContentstackLivePreview from "@contentstack/live-preview-utils"` plus a module-level `ContentstackLivePreview.init(...)`. That file is transitively imported by `next.config.source.ts` (via `redirectsService`), which `npm run build:config` bundles into the CommonJS `next.config.js` with `esbuild --external:./node_modules/*`. Because `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` is `"type": "module"` (ESM-first exports), esbuild emitted a bare `require("…/dist/modern/index.js")` of an ESM file. `src/setupTests.ts` does `require("../next.config")`, so Jest hit `import` statements it can't parse → all 247 suites failed with "Jest encountered an unexpected token".

## Fix (moved Live Preview init to client-side, per the failure analyst)
- **`src/services/contentstack.ts`** — removed the static `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` import and the module-level `init`. Kept the `live_preview` block in the Delivery SDK `options` (`enable`/`host`/`management_token`, conditionally spread so `string|undefined` never lands in the required `string` fields) and the three new env vars in the destructure.
- **`src/context/contentstackContext.tsx`** — `ContentstackContextProvider` now lazily initializes the SDK **client-side only** via dynamic `import()` of both `services/contentstack` (for `Stack`) and `@contentstack/live-preview-utils`, then registers `onEntryChange(() => setContent(prev => ({...prev})))`. Per Contentstack docs `onEntryChange` takes no arguments — the re-render relies on the SDK's internal state update, propagated through the existing `useContent`/`getContentByKey` pipeline without a page reload. Dynamic import keeps both modules out of `next.config.js` **and** out of the `_app` client chunk's static graph (avoids the module-level env throw in the browser). A `try/catch` + `typeof window` guard keeps published content rendering normally when Live Preview is inactive.
- **`src/pages/_app.tsx`, `src/pages/404.tsx`, `src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx`** — unchanged from the prior attempt (already render the provider / wire `useContent`).
- **`.env.local.sample`** — unchanged from the prior attempt (documents `CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_ENABLED`, `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST`, `CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN`).

